WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.300
After getting everybody's hopes raised over
the weekend with the release of a surprise

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:10.190
teaser, the truth behind the Danny McBride-starring
Crocodile Dundee reboot has been discovered...and

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:11.410
it's all a lie.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:15.700
An investigation conducted by the Brisbane
Times has uncovered that the movie is nothing

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:19.349
more than a viral marketing stunt for Tourism
Australia.

00:00:19.349 --> 00:00:24.650
The "movie" was initially announced on Friday
in an exclusive report by People, which featured

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:28.910
deceptive quotes from McBride and Paul Hogan,
the original movies' Mick Dundee.

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:32.600
"That's not a knife.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.620
That's a knife."

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:37.930
Hogan said in the People reveal,

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:41.840
"Throughout the past few years, I've been
thinking about how to bring Dundee to a new

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:42.840
generation.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:47.219
I'm excited to introduce the new Crocodile
Dundee to the world and look forward to sharing

00:00:47.219 --> 00:00:49.670
more news about those involved very soon."

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:55.630
Hogan previously served as a Australia tourism
pitchman in 1984 with the "G'Day Mate" campaign,

00:00:55.630 --> 00:01:00.219
which continues to inform just about every
stereotypical view Americans hold of the land

00:01:00.219 --> 00:01:01.219
down under.

00:01:01.219 --> 00:01:06.613
"Come and say good day and I'll slip an extra
shrimp on the barbie for ya."

00:01:06.613 --> 00:01:11.250
The initial Dundee trailer was met with skepticism
from the start by many commentators in the

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:16.570
entertainment industry, who questioned how
a movie with an IMDB-estimated budget of $30

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:22.210
million and the involvement of such busy performers
as McBride and Chris Hemsworth could've been

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:23.930
made in absolute secrecy.

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:28.270
While Hemsworth's involvement in the movie's
second teaser appeared to add some credibility

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:32.740
to the project, others noticed the curious
fact that Hemsworth is currently employed

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:34.640
as a Tourism Australia ambassador.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:38.259
That was enough to convince many that the
movie wasn't quite on the level.

00:01:38.259 --> 00:01:41.549
Thanks to the Brisbane Times, that theory
has now been all-but-proven.

00:01:41.549 --> 00:01:45.360
Alas, poor Dundee—we hardly knew ye.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:49.310
Everybody pour out a little Bundaberg for
the summer we could've had.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:51.380
"G'day, losers."

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:52.380
Thanks for watching!

